    "result_text": "Only one test class exists in the repo, and it's green. The build passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature end-to-end. The opt-in flag already existed (it skipped the duplicate-household rejection); the missing piece was assigning and returning a shared, stable `householdId`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `householdId` property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and it's returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}`), and refined the `sharesHousehold` description.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `householdId` field (`@Column(name = \"household_id\")`) with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it into `OwnerDto` automatically by name.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added a `household_id` column to `owners` in the hsqldb, h2, mysql, and postgres schema files, and appended the corresponding value to the positional seed inserts in hsqldb `data.sql` (the one used by tests; h2 uses named columns already).\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 When `sharesHousehold` is true, it now calls a new `joinHousehold(lastName, address)` helper that:\n   - Derives a **stable, deterministic** id from the normalized (trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, lower-cased) last name + address \u2014 the upper-cased first 12 hex chars of their SHA-256 digest, so every member of the same household resolves to the identical value.\n   - Back-fills any existing same-household owners with that id and persists them, so the whole household agrees (\"assign both the same householdId\").\n   - Sets it on the joining owner before save.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` passes: two owners joining an existing same-lastName/same-address owner via `sharesHousehold` receive an identical, non-blank `householdId`.",
